WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.233
Virtual environments.

2
00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:06.591
Every Python project deserves its own private set of packages.

3
00:00:06.591 --> 00:00:07.900
Here's why, and how.

4
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:15.067
A virtual environment is a per-project interpreter with its own folder of installed packages.

5
00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:19.600
Activating it simply points your shell's PATH at that project's python and pip.

6
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.100
The iron rule: never install into the system Python.

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.367
Here's the payoff.

8
00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:29.967
Project A keeps numpy one point twenty six in its own environment.

9
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:32.767
Project B keeps numpy two point one.

10
00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:36.367
They coexist peacefully, because neither can see the other.

11
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:39.300
The lifecycle has four steps.

12
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.933
Create the environment as a folder named dot venv.

13
00:00:43.233 --> 00:00:46.100
Activate it, so your shell uses its python and pip.

14
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.833
Anything you install now lives only inside that folder.

15
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.233
Deactivate, and you're back to the system.

16
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:54.900
Let's prove it in a terminal.

17
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.533
We create an environment and activate it.

18
00:00:57.833 --> 00:01:02.167
Then install httpx, and it lands only in this environment.

19
00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:05.526
After deactivating, importing httpx fails.

20
00:01:05.526 --> 00:01:08.367
That failure shows the isolation works.

21
00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.272
The modern tool is uv.

22
00:01:10.272 --> 00:01:12.533
Same idea, dramatically faster.

23
00:01:13.733 --> 00:01:14.700
A real case.

24
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.267
Your RAG service is pinned below numpy two by a legacy faiss build.

25
00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:23.033
Your exoplanet classifier wants numpy two point one.

26
00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:25.656
Two environments, zero conflict.

27
00:01:25.656 --> 00:01:29.867
Later, a Dockerfile is the same idea frozen into an image.

28
00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:31.821
Let's recap.

29
00:01:31.821 --> 00:01:35.967
A virtual environment is a private interpreter and package folder.

30
00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:38.267
Activation just changes your PATH.

31
00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:40.467
Uv is the fast modern tool.

32
00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.565
And never install into the system Python.

33
00:01:43.565 --> 00:01:46.500
Next up: packaging with pyproject dot toml.
